tip: | Look at the fire. | The stones sit in a 2:1 ellipse and the logs run along the grid. Only the flame ignores the grid, because it is the one thing here that moves.
tip: 3 | A flame is one ramp. | Red-orange outside, yellow inside, almost white at the heart. Each tongue is the same shape, a step lighter and a size smaller.
tip: | Try it. | The light on the ground is a checker, then sparser dots, with nothing blended. Dither a wider ring and the fire looks brighter. | dither
